*Context: *Last month, to explore the public=E2=80=99s usage habits and att=
itudes
toward generative AI, Tencent Research Institute conducted an online survey
of 3,570 Chinese adults (link to *original Chinese
<https://substack.com/redirect/9cd8d4d8-1cdd-4b31-a167-aa2618d4880a?j=3DeyJ=
1IjoiMmZseDYifQ.6O_iC1_GWCzChnbrHzSrs1hMpJpoODTUJm_FAk3tf6E>*).
This is not a nationally representative survey; rather, it captures the
views of highly educated young adults. To make this clear, 85% of the
survey respondents had a college degree or higher, whereas just 10% of
China=E2=80=99s labor force (age 25-64) has at least a bachelor=E2=80=99s d=
egree. They did
collect a gender-balanced sample from a variety of industries, so the below
findings probably reflect the views of young, highly educated digital
natives in China.

*Key Takeaways: Adoption patterns =E2=80=94 wide, localized, but =E2=80=9Cw=
ait-and-see=E2=80=9D
attitude regarding willingness to pay. *Let=E2=80=99s go through these thre=
e points
in turn.

   -

   96% of respondents had used AI-generated content tools, with two-thirds
   (67.7%) of those being daily users.
   -

   Chinese companies accounted for the top three most-used products:
   ByteDance=E2=80=99s Doubao, DeepSeek, and Tencent Yuanbao. Tencent Resea=
rch
   Institute attributes this trend to network access restrictions (e.g., yo=
u
   have to find mirror sites or use a VPN to access Claude or ChatGPT),
   superior Chinese-language capabilities of local services, and synergies
   with the ecosystem of Chinese applications (e.g., *WeChat=E2=80=99s inte=
gration
   of DeepSeek
   <https://substack.com/redirect/0c732e13-d93d-432c-bd69-0afedb9e58dc?j=3D=
eyJ1IjoiMmZseDYifQ.6O_iC1_GWCzChnbrHzSrs1hMpJpoODTUJm_FAk3tf6E>*
   )
   -

      I was disappointed that the survey results don=E2=80=99t show the act=
ual bar
      graphs for this question; instead, they just provide a word cloud, wh=
ich
      omits the exact figures for the most popular generative AI apps.
      -

      Two more interesting points about age groups and GenAI product usage.
      =E2=80=9CAmong respondents aged 20-29, ChatGPT=E2=80=99s usage rate w=
as significantly
      higher than among respondents in other age groups,=E2=80=9D the artic=
le states.
      And, Moonshot AI=E2=80=99s Kimi places in the top three among
respondents under 20.
      -

      In the section on commercialization prospects, the Tencent Research
      Institute survey found that about 60% of respondents stated that
they were
      =E2=80=9Cwatching from the sidelines [=E6=AD=A3=E5=9C=A8=E8=A7=82=E6=
=9C=9B], but would pay if it=E2=80=99s good=E2=80=9D
(see image
      below). Among the users that were open to paying for generative AI
      services, the most preferred payment option was =E2=80=9Cmonthly
payment=E2=80=9D and under
      100 RMB/month. The study authors theorizes that consumers see the
      generative AI product market like video streaming services (for conte=
xt,
      the monthly fee for iQiyi [China=E2=80=99s Netflix] is around 25 RMB/=
month).

