On September 30, the Department of Education ended seven decades of
(bipartisan) support for initiatives such as the National Resource Center
(NRCs) program, dedicated to language and area studies. GW has two NRCs,
including one that supports students to pursue intensive language study in
East Asia. Again, what are we doing here? Reporting for *Inside Higher Ed*,
Johanna Alonso provides the broader context.
